Theo Jansen : I want to put these forms of life on the beaches .
And they should survive over there , on their own , in the future .
Learning to live on their own -- and it &apos;ll take couple of more years to let them walk on their own .
The mechanical beasts will not get their energy from food , but from the wind .
The wind will move feathers on their back , which will drive their feet .
The beast walks sideways on the wet sand of the beach , with its nose pointed into the wind .
